msgid "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ):"
msgstr ""

msgid "How to add a new coin to the widget?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Go to the \"Coin List\" tab in settings and use the search bar by name or ticker (btc, eth, sol), or use batch adding separated by dots (btc.eth.sol)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What does \"Rate limit exceeded\" mean?"
msgstr ""

msgid "The free public CoinGecko API has a request limit per minute. If this limit is exceeded, the widget automatically enables a 60-second protective countdown timer and will resume updating data after it finishes."
msgstr ""

msgid "How do system notifications (Alerts) work?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the \"Alerts\" tab, you can set up triggers for coins reaching specific prices, 24h high/low breakouts, ATH/ATL reach, as well as macro indicators (Fear & Greed index shifts, BTC/ETH dominance, etc.)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Why does the panel indicator status change?"
msgstr ""

msgid "The indicator on the Plasma panel reflects the real-time overall state of the crypto market (e.g. panic/correction, rally/growth, flat/accumulation, altseason)."
msgstr ""

msgid "How to select an individual card for the desktop?"
msgstr ""

msgid "When placing the widget directly on the desktop (desktop mode), open \"General Settings\" and choose one of the 16 card types (Coin Card, Fear & Greed Index, Global Market Cap, BTC Halving, ETH/BTC, Rainbow Zone, etc.)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where does the widget fetch price data from?"
msgstr ""

msgid "The widget receives current price quotes from the CoinGecko API, and the Fear & Greed Index from the Alternative.me API."
msgstr ""

msgid "Does the widget work without an internet connection?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Searching and adding coins work offline thanks to a local SQLite database. An active internet connection is required to update real-time prices."
msgstr ""
